@tradition pick-your-own
// Wednesdays 06:15, the garden. The gardeners leave baskets out and crew pick fruit straight off the racks to take to
// breakfast.
== mail
- Pick-your-own breakfast tomorrow at {time} in the garden. Baskets by the door. Take what's ripe and carry it up.
== ask
- Pick your own in the garden tomorrow. Fresh fruit for breakfast.
- Baskets are out in the garden in the morning. Come early.
== here
- This one's ripe. Smell it.
- Only the ripe ones. The gardeners are watching.   #funny
- Best breakfast of the week, this.
== thanks
- In the garden you fill a basket with fruit straight off the racks and carry it up to breakfast.   #warm
== chatter
- Pick your own tomorrow. Get there before the gym lot.   #funny
- Fruit off the rack tastes different. Better.
- The garden smells amazing on pick-your-own day.
